This document presents a comprehensive adversarial analysis of three deployment strategies for the Atlas Delta real-time anomaly scoring API. The service must handle 12k requests/second with a p95 latency target under 120ms. Previous incidents revealed critical vulnerabilities: configuration drift, slow cold-start warm-up, and insufficient rollback validation.

---

